    "agent_query": "Read AGENT_TASK.md and README_AGENT.md before changing code. A correct but unoptimised four-stage TileLang implementation of the Mamba-2 SSD forward is already in candidates/kernel_v001. Make it faster without changing what it computes, over the whole declared support domain (any batch 1-16, any positive L, any H up to 256 with any G dividing H, P a multiple of 16 up to 256, N a power of two from 16 to 256): the internal chunk size, the staging of intermediates, tiling, layouts, pipelining, and fusion are all yours to choose. Your score comes from hidden test cases in four workload families (batch, serving, long context, and layers captured from real models); their shapes differ from the public tests, which cover the same four families. Your final result is the best valid score you reach within the time budget, so keep versioned candidates and leave FINAL_VERSION on your strongest clean candidate. Evaluate candidates only by the feedback from the public tests and your submissions. Submitted compute must stay in TileLang: torch may only allocate buffers and create views, and every evaluation records the torch operators a call dispatches and rejects anything else. Before each manual submission, wait for all public-test and compiler workers to exit, then run sforge-submit --details; each Judge run takes about half an hour of your budget. Before finishing, run the full public suite once on the selected version:\n\n```bash\ntools/run_public_tests.sh --candidate-version N\n```\n\nDo not copy external implementations or solution material into your submission."
  },
